[36m(TaskRunner pid=160284)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=160284)[0m 1. First, we calculate the combined speed at which Alicia and Beth are closing the gap between them. Since Alicia is biking at 18 miles per hour and Beth is biking at 12 miles per hour, their combined speed is \(18 + 12 = 30\) miles per hour.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=160284)[0m 2. Next, we calculate the time it takes for them to meet. Since they are 45 miles apart and they are closing the gap at 30 miles per hour, the time it takes for them to meet is \( \frac{45 \text{ miles}}{30 \text{ miles per hour}} = 1.5 \text{ hours} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=160284)[0m 3. Finally, we calculate how far Alicia has traveled in 1.5 hours. Since Alicia is biking at 18 miles per hour, in 1.5 hours she will have traveled \(18 \text{ miles per hour} \times 1.5 \text{ hours} = 27 \text{ miles}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=160284)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=160284)[0m So, Alicia and Beth will meet 27 miles from City \(A\).
